WEBVTT

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:31.110
Hey, Rikiishi.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.080
You'd better hurry up, or you'll miss tonight's main event.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.670
Main event? Who's fighting?

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:39.080
Who's fighting? Inoue of Asia Gym.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:40.500
Inoue?

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.080
Hey, pull yourself together! He's your next opponent!

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:47.080
Enough.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.480
There's only one opponent for me now.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.250
Only one.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.850
And he's not a main eventer yet.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.830
This is what we've been waiting for! It's the No Guard tactic!

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.160
Show us the Cross Counter!

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.690
What's the matter, Zawada!?

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.720
Can't you move when you're cornered!?

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.870
Great job! That makes three victories in a row, Joe!

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:07.140
What you meant to say was "three consecutive KO's."

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:07.960
Ain't that right, old man?

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:10.960
I told you to stop using the No Guard tactic.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.970
Well, I gotta give the audience what they want. Don't you agree, old man?

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.970
Okay, everyone! I'm gonna whale on some guy named Toyama Juzo next; make sure you're there!

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.470
We're looking forward to it!

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.640
It's good that you're winning, but at least make it last three rounds next time!

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.190
You can count on me!

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:31.830
Knock 'em outta the park!

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:37.170
And now, we shall begin tonight's main event—

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:38.450
Huh?

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.880
Man, that was fun.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.450
Hey, wait! I'm coming too!

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.240
P-Please don't leave your seats!

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.700
The matches aren't over yet!

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.210
You're kidding, right? We only came here to see Yabuki Joe!

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:52.210
That's right! Stop putting on these boring main events!

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:56.670
Hurry it up!

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.670
<i>This is boring!</i>

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:00.470
How can this be?

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.720
There are more spectators for a six-round opener than the main event!

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.820
So, you came to see Yabuki, after all.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:25.080
Joe did it again, didn't he?

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.330
I've just about had enough of his Cross Counter.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:32.330
More importantly, shouldn't you have stayed to watch your next opponent's fight?

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:35.830
Didn't you watch his fight for me?

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:42.560
If you left halfway through, that means he must not have been worth watching.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.560
Or were you only there for the opening match?

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.340
Please don't put it like that.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:51.850
I'm not thinking about my next match, Miss.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.420
I'm thinking about a future match.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.820
With Yabuki Joe?

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.410
Ow! Stop pushing me, asshole!

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.210
Keep it down, Joe!

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:18.050
That's enough outta you, old man! I won today! It was my third consecutive KO!

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:18.920
What about it?

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:19.950
Ow!

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:23.420
You could've at least called me a taxi to take me home!

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:27.930
What are you talking about? Standing on a crowded train is a good way to train!

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.180
Enough of this.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:31.930
I'm all worn out from my match.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:32.930
I can't stand up anymore!

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:35.010
Joe!

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:36.890
Molester!

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.690
Bad news! Bad news, bad news, bad news!

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:43.900
What's going on?

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:45.270
What is it?

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.910
Did something happen to Bro Joe?

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.410
Come on, tell us!

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:54.580
T-Truth is...

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.920
Bro Joe's getting married!

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.690
What?

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:01.170
I-It's true! The electrician told me!

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.170
Hey, this better not be a joke!

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:05.070
Of course it's not!

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:09.180
I saw them moving brand new women's appliances into Tange Gym!

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:11.500
Women's appliances?

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.220
That lowlife!

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.560
What do you think, Sir? Doesn't it just scream "newlywed" to you?

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:22.190
Good stuff, good stuff.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:24.690
So, when's the ceremony?

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:25.950
Ceremony?

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.760
That's obvious. It's on the next red-letter day.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.700
More importantly, what about the rice cooker?

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.200
I got it right here! Here you go!

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:37.690
Now this is great!

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:39.710
I'm having trouble believing this is all free!

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:43.590
Well, I wish you both happiness!

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.510
Thanks!

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:46.640
Drive safely!

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:50.680
Lecher!

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:55.450
You no-good, perverted womanizer!

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:58.430
Huh, what the hell? What's the matter?

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:01.810
Bro, are you sure you should get married while you're training?

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:03.520
So, who is she?

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:19.850
What? You didn't have to smirk and laugh at me like that!

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:25.930
That electrician offers 10% off to newlyweds and he throws in a free rice cooker.

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:27.960
So, I just used my head.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.970
What's with your hands?

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:44.480
I just... uh... got excited...

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:45.940
Do you now think I'm weird?

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:47.940
You moron!

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.490
How could you buy this without consulting me?

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:52.700
Now, now, old man.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:56.500
This washing machine and refrigerator are for your own comfort!

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:00.940
If you think about it, this is me fulfilling my duty to my coach!

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:03.700
But, Joe, how did you pay for it?

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:04.830
Oh, you see...

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:07.620
They're gonna come collect it soon.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.010
Wh-What?

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.010
You moron! Where are you keeping the money to pay them?

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:16.510
Come on, don't be so miserly, old man.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:19.020
Miserly? Me?

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.630
Well, I've gotten three consecutive KO's since my debut.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:25.790
My fight money should be rolling in.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.490
So, why can't I spend some of it?

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:28.990
You gotta be kidding!

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:33.490
Do you even know how little you earn from six-round matches!?

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:35.500
He's right, Joe.

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:39.490
That's why he's still working as a day laborer.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:46.720
So, even though I've gone pro, and I've got three straight KO's to my name,

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:48.000
we're still as poor as ever?

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.010
Joe...

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:51.440
So...

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:55.010
Even though my punches can floor someone,

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.010
they can't even buy us a rice cooker?

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.500
Of course not!

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:00.740
Being a professional isn't that easy!

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:03.480
You've only won three matches and now you're acting like royalty?

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.770
S-Say that again, you old geezer!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.200
S-Stop, Joe!

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.240
Evening!

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:11.490
That must be the electrician...

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:14.240
Don't worry. I'll shoo him off.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:20.950
Wh-Who are you?

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:25.460
Um, can I become a member of this gym?

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:26.960
A member?

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:30.960
Yes. I want to become a boxer like Yabuki Joe-san.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.870
I'm sorry, but I refuse.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:37.890
I can't handle any more than Joe and Nishi.

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:43.250
Hey, old man, one more won't hurt!

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.200
Right, Nishi?

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:47.190
Sure. It's a little lonely with only two pupils here.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:51.830
I see. If you think it's a good idea, I'll think it over.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.150
R-Really?

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.660
But my fees are pretty high.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.160
How much?

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:00.910
A hundred thousand yen.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:02.960
A hundred thousand yen?

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.150
But, Nishi...

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:34.150
I guess it's true that money makes the world go round, huh?

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:38.650
I'm talking about the hundred thousand yen.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.570
Thanks to him, we can pay the electrician.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.660
And with another trainee or two on board,

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.120
the old man won't have to do his day laboring anymore!

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:48.120
You're the biggest fool I know.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:54.400
What kinda moron would pay a hundred thousand yen to a run-down gym like ours?

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.130
That's just stupid!

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:57.730
One, two! One, two!

00:10:57.730 --> 00:10:59.140
Say what you want. He'll come!

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:03.400
After all, it's my strength he admires!

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:10.500
Go home.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:12.990
But...

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:14.150
I have the hundred thousand...

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:19.330
It's my fault. I didn't think you would readily give me so much money.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.160
Um, would 150,000 yen do?

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.760
It's not a matter of money.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:23.660
Look.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.330
There's no nail up there to hang your card on.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:29.660
I don't take trainees.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:33.860
If you really want to box, you should find another gym.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:37.970
Forget the hundred thousand; they'll take you in for ten.

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:41.680
B-But I want to join this gym!

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.680
I'm sorry to say this, but I cannot fulfill your wishes.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.340
Hey, Joe! Hold up!

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:54.360
Look over there!

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.110
Isn't that the guy from last night?

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:00.280
Th-That's our hundred thousand!

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.750
Old man! Old man!

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:05.930
Old man!

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:09.860
Old man, did Mr. Hundred Thousand drop by?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:11.850
He did.

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:13.180
So, did he bring the money?

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:14.330
Yeah, he brought it.

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:16.930
I'm so happy!

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:19.340
A-Are you serious, old man?

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:22.340
Yeah, he brought it with him all right.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:25.350
Hear that, Nishi? Today's such a great day!

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.850
But he took it home with him.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:30.100
Wh-What? What's that supposed to mean, old man?

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:31.600
Shut up!

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:36.980
He failed my entrance test.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:37.610
Test?

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:41.400
If he turned tail and ran after hearing the fee was a hundred thousand yen...

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.130
he'd lose points for cowardice.

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.620
But, he brought it, didn't he?

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:49.120
What's worse is to come back with the full hundred grand.

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.100
I don't understand.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:55.060
Boxing is a hungry sport.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:58.590
The fights are between hungry strays.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:03.720
Never in its history has a well-to-do child become a champion.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:08.110
Anyone who can produce a hundred thousand yen just like that...

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:09.850
won't amount to anything.

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:12.850
Good morning, Sir.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.950
Thank you.

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:17.820
Did you gentlemen hear that? That's the way it is.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:19.400
Understand?

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:21.100
I see. I understand.

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:23.860
But, old man, how are you gonna pay the electrician?

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:26.120
I couldn't care less about that.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.050
What's the matter, Joe?

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:49.150
It's nothing.

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:51.060
If only we had that hundred thousand yen...

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:53.890
There's nothing we can do about it. We don't have what we don't have.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:57.560
Well, we'll just have to earn an honest buck and pay him back a little each month.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:00.320
'Scuse me, we're from Hayashi Grocery!

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:05.060
Hey, wait, Joe! Where are you going?

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:06.690
Back to the gym.

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:10.000
I might come up with a good idea by pummeling the sandbag.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:11.700
Joe!

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:15.710
The grocer's wife is gonna yell at me again!

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:31.680
Yabuki-san!

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.580
H-Hey.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:37.480
You've come here again?

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:40.460
Uh, I know this may seem a little presumptuous,

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:41.480
but here.

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:43.750
Th-This is...

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.030
the receipt from the electrician!

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:51.750
Yeah, he came to collect his payment while you were out, so I paid for it.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:56.000
In return, could you coach me without letting your chairman know?

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.250
Well, that's rich folk for ya!

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:03.130
What? Did he get lost while taking customers' orders?

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:06.130
Well, um, his bike got a flat...

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:08.130
That's the third time you've used that excuse!

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:10.120
Sorry. You're quite right.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:14.300
Mother, you should cut him some slack! Yabuki-kun had a match yesterday!

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:18.100
If only his fatigue from yesterday was enough to settle him down for good!

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.120
I-I'll go check on him!

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.360
I'll go, too!

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:35.310
Good job! You've got potential!

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:36.290
Really?

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.770
It's fine.

00:15:40.770 --> 00:15:43.670
I fell over just like that the first time I punched the sandbag.

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.170
Really?

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:48.200
Really.

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.690
Now, continue. Continue.

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:52.130
Yes!

00:15:56.770 --> 00:15:59.060
Good! Magnificent!

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.140
You're outstanding!

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:07.150
Great! Anyway, you're really good!

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:19.500
All right, let's leave it at that for today.

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:21.970
Yes! Thank you so much!

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:25.460
Don't mention it. Come again tomorrow!

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:26.490
Joe!

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:28.510
Well, if it isn't Nishi-kun!

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:30.080
Ow! What are you doing, Nishi?

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:34.600
Hey, Joe! What do you think you're doing?

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.470
Couldn't you tell? I was doing some private tutoring.

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:39.520
But the old man said...

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:41.970
Don't be such a stiff.

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:43.520
He won't know if we don't tell him.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:47.020
I'm in his debt for paying the electrician.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.080
Wh-What? You...

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:52.090
It's fine, it's fine. After all, he's just a lazy rich kid—

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:52.990
Coach Yabuki!

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:55.730
Yes, yes, yes, yes?

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.490
I mean...

00:16:58.070 --> 00:16:59.040
What is it?

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:01.390
I'm looking forward to tomorrow!

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:04.590
You did well today.

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:11.300
He called me Coach!

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:27.360
What is it?

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:30.860
To box, you need courage, guts, tenacity, wild instincts,

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:33.860
and above all, a sturdy body.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:37.830
Are you brave enough to undergo one of my examinations?

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:43.290
Man, being a coach is tiring!

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:46.290
You're so stuck up!

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:49.290
I think so, too.

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:51.300
Oh?

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:56.300
It's a savings passbook!

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.300
It must be his!

00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:03.310
Really? Guess he must've dropped it when he was changing.

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.350
Well, that's rich kids for you.

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:08.520
H-He's not rich!

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:10.250
Look!

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:13.710
He's been saving up his money over three years,

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:15.260
and finally hit a hundred thousand yen!

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:17.290
Th-That hundred thousand...

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:19.440
was all he had!

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.290
C-Can I see that, Nishi-kun?

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:29.650
Ishikura Osamu. Nakano Ward, Ekota, 4-37, Wakakusa Printing Office.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:31.050
He's a live-in employee!

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:37.420
You moron!

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:41.120
How could you be so underhanded?

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:44.060
You're just... just...

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.860
You took all the money he'd saved up!

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:50.020
But, old man, I thought he was just a lazy rich kid...

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:52.660
Say that again, you bastard!

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:55.090
Old man, you should forgive Yabuki-kun.

00:18:55.090 --> 00:19:00.530
Yabuki-kun only bought the washing machine and refrigerator so you could have an easier life.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:01.630
Chief!

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:03.540
Please forgive him!

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:09.000
Come with me. We're going to go apologize.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.040
Ishikura? Yes, he's here.

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:19.010
Hey, Ishikura! You've got guests!

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:21.800
Yabuki-san!

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.320
It's my responsibility.

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:32.850
The electrician wouldn't take back the appliances...

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.770
so this is all I can give back to you today.

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:40.710
I-I'm sorry.

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:43.730
I got the wrong idea about you.

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:45.240
I'm truly sorry.

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:53.090
I love boxing, and I used to go see matches all the time.

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:56.930
But I never once considered entering the ring myself...

00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:58.880
until I watched your bout, Yabuki-san.

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:02.620
When I saw your fight,

00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:05.290
it felt like something inside me had awakened!

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:09.570
That's right. The sensation of my blood boiling made me want to get in there, too!

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:14.900
I quickly grew bored of setting type in a dark corner of a printing press.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:17.900
I'm a man! I had to do it!

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:21.910
It's the other way around. Joe's the wretched one here.

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.990
You can dream of becoming a boxer.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:30.190
You can also dream of opening your own printing press.

00:20:30.190 --> 00:20:31.930
You can pursue either dream.

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:36.920
But Joe has nothing but boxing in his head.

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:40.450
Joe's only dream is to become a champion.

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:42.850
Actually, it's not so much a dream,

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:48.100
but his destiny. In other words, if you took boxing away from him, he'd have nothing left.

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:54.580
That's why he fights in a way that stimulates people like you.

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:58.400
Yabuki-san, when's your next match?

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:03.400
Uh, well... The third of next month.

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:04.810
That right?

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:09.410
All right! Then, I'll stand at your side of the ring, and cheer you on at the top of my voice!

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:22.720
I've decided to just watch the bouts.

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:25.650
Dr. Oigawa told me that...

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:28.060
I don't have the physique to be a boxer.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:45.800
Wow! There's no smog tonight!

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:51.930
Y-You...

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:55.610
You shouldn't even listen to that quack!

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:58.750
C-Come back tomorrow! I'll coach you again!

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:02.190
Yabuki-san, please don't worry about me anymore.

00:22:02.190 --> 00:22:05.320
You should use the time to train harder and harder,

00:22:05.320 --> 00:22:08.760
and win your next match with an amazing KO!

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:14.430
Well, I'll be. You sound just like the old man!

00:22:44.870 --> 00:22:46.490
Sure is cold out, huh, Nishi-kun?

00:22:46.490 --> 00:22:48.720
You said it. Winter's just around the corner.

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:51.180
Yeah, we should hail a taxi sometime.

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:51.950
Ain't that right?

00:22:51.950 --> 00:22:54.140
Whoa, now! Don't go wasting our money!

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:56.270
Old man, I'm fine with the bus.

00:22:58.520 --> 00:23:00.230
We should live frugally for a while.

00:23:01.770 --> 00:23:04.280
Like that guy with his savings passbook. Right?

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:16.060
Wolf...

00:23:17.770 --> 00:23:18.890
Rikiishi...

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:22.550
Just you wait.

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:27.760
I'm gonna win every single one of my matches,

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:29.880
and climb the ladder to the ring where you're waiting!

00:23:39.780 --> 00:23:42.090
Nishi's record isn't getting any better,

00:23:42.090 --> 00:23:46.910
so he puts his all into training for the next match.

00:23:46.910 --> 00:23:47.900
But...

00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:50.140
As Nishi steps into the ring with that determination,

00:23:50.140 --> 00:23:51.910
he's down before he knows it!

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:57.050
As Nishi falls, he sees Joe crying instead of yelling at him.

00:23:57.050 --> 00:24:00.700
Now, as Joe sheds warm tears of friendship,

00:24:00.700 --> 00:24:02.960
which way is tomorrow!?
